    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's better, but I'm still not quite there. It still feels a bit like \"corporate speak.\" I feel like I need something with a bit more character—something that acknowledges he has a bit of a \"free spirit\" or a \"quirky\" side, which is part of why our clients like him so much. Maybe you could use a little bit of metaphor or some more colorful language to describe how his occasional tardiness might disrupt the \"magic\" or the \"flow\" of the team? Just something that makes the feedback feel more human and less like a handbook.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Harkening back to the spirit of a free-spirited individual, you can weave in a metaphor that speaks to the energy of the team. It's about capturing that unique spark he brings, but ensuring it doesn't derail the morning momentum.\n\nHere is a draft leaning into that more colorful, human approach:\n\n\"Marcus, your knack for keeping clients delighted is pure gold—it's a genuine talent, and it really shines through in your results. You bring a wonderful, vibrant energy to the sales floor, much like a charismatic, slightly unpredictable leader. To make sure that magic flows seamlessly across the whole team, we need to ensure you're present right at the start of our morning huddle. When you join us right on time, it helps us lock into that initial momentum, keeping our whole team's energy vibrant and focused from the jump.\"",
      "source": "target",
